<section data-expansion style="padding:0 0 130px"><div class="narrow">
<h2 class="disp" style="font-size:clamp(34px,4vw,52px);margin:0 0 28px;max-width:860px">What a technical SEO audit finds, and what we do about it</h2>
<p class="p" style="font-size:18px;margin:0 0 22px">Technical problems are the quiet ones. A store can have good products, good copy and good links, and still lose visits because Google can't reach or read the right pages. These problems rarely show up in the store itself, so most owners don't know they exist.</p>
<p class="label red" style="margin:36px 0 14px">The common technical problems</p>
<ul style="margin:0 0 26px;padding-left:22px;font-size:18px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--ink2)"><li style="margin:0 0 8px"><strong style="color:var(--ink)">Pages Google can't reach.</strong> Products that sit deep in the site, with no links pointing to them.</li><li style="margin:0 0 8px"><strong style="color:var(--ink)">Pages that shouldn't be indexed.</strong> Filter combinations and internal search results that add noise without adding value.</li><li style="margin:0 0 8px"><strong style="color:var(--ink)">Redirect chains and broken links.</strong> Each extra step slows the page and wastes the search signal.</li><li style="margin:0 0 8px"><strong style="color:var(--ink)">Duplicate pages.</strong> The same product in several collections, with several URLs competing with each other.</li><li style="margin:0 0 8px"><strong style="color:var(--ink)">Slow templates.</strong> A theme that loads heavy code on every page.</li></ul>
<p class="label red" style="margin:36px 0 14px">How we find them</p>
<p class="p" style="font-size:18px;margin:0 0 22px">We crawl the store the way a search engine does, and compare the results with Google Search Console. We look at which pages are indexed, which aren't, and why. We check speed on real devices, and we review the structured data.</p>
<p class="label red" style="margin:36px 0 14px">How we fix them</p>
<p class="p" style="font-size:18px;margin:0 0 22px">We rank each problem by how much traffic and revenue it likely affects, and fix the most important ones first. Each fix is tested, and we check the results in the next crawl.</p>
<h3 class="disp" style="font-size:clamp(32px,3.6vw,44px);margin:56px 0 24px">Frequently asked questions</h3>
<div style="border-top:1px solid var(--ink);margin:0 0 20px"><details style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);padding:24px 0"><summary style="font-size:20px;font-weight:600;cursor:pointer">Do we need developer access?</summary><p class="p" style="margin:14px 0 0">Often, yes. Some technical fixes need changes to the theme or site code. We'll tell you what's needed and who should make the change.</p></details><details style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);padding:24px 0"><summary style="font-size:20px;font-weight:600;cursor:pointer">How long does a technical audit take?</summary><p class="p" style="margin:14px 0 0">Most stores can be crawled and reviewed in one to two weeks. The fixes that follow depend on the size of the store.</p></details></div>
</div></section>
